---
import StudyLayout from "../../../layouts/StudyLayout.astro";

const review = {
  slug: "gravity-coil-fx-2026-11-03",
  title: "Gravity coil FX — study-quality review",
  status: "accepted" as const,
  phase: "scope" as const,
  question:
    "Evidence and remaining limits of the accepted gravity-collection trial.",
};
const rows = [
  [
    "Purpose",
    "Supported",
    "The study connects gravity becoming potential to readable light alongside engine FX.",
  ],
  [
    "Investigation",
    "Supported",
    "Static alternatives progressed to a real powered flyby, then two coils and a turn through the field.",
  ],
  [
    "Alternatives and reasoning",
    "Supported",
    "Lines, Capture and condensed bright variants were rejected. Soft dispersed grains, larger size and original offset survived review.",
  ],
  [
    "Evidence fit",
    "Partial",
    "The flyby supports visual review. Collection, capacity, replay and force invariance have unit coverage; long-run balance and device performance remain unproven.",
  ],
  [
    "Cumulative agreement",
    "Supported",
    "The owner approved purple J at 250%, double size, original offset and additive light, then confirmed 1 energy/s per coil and full-storage shutoff.",
  ],
  [
    "Design coherence",
    "Supported",
    "The same shared fold and transparent additive FX surface serve fitted game flight and the Lab. Activity follows actual collection.",
  ],
  [
    "Remaining uncertainty",
    "Partial",
    "The alpha rate and 0.25-second activity fade still need play review; overlapping wells use nearest-planet visual direction without multiplying output.",
  ],
  [
    "Integration implications",
    "Supported",
    "Parts 03–04 identify power accounting, shared rendering, catalog, spec and verification work. No storage migration or gravity tuning is required.",
  ],
];
---

<StudyLayout study={review}>
  <section>
    <h2>Evidence assessment</h2>
    <p>
      This agent assessment is separate from the owner’s acceptance of the
      visual treatment and collection rule. It does not claim human approval of
      long-run balance or the implementation’s new fade.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/lab/studies/gravity-coil-fx-2026-11-03#planet-flight"
        >Accepted flyby and parts 03–04</a
      >
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Criterion</th>
          <th>Assessment</th>
          <th>Evidence / limits</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {rows.map(([criterion, assessment, evidence]) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{criterion}</td>
            <td>{assessment}</td>
            <td>{evidence}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Local implementation evidence</h2>
    <p>
      Collection and shared flight rendering are implemented. Browser inspection
      confirmed two coils collecting 2.0 energy/s with purple FX during the
      turning flyby. The catalog/persistence/test-flight browser check passed.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contracts, types and all unit tests passed in local verification run
      <code>2026-11-03T09-58-44.023Z-1l12uW</code>. That partial run failed
      repository-wide formatting on the pre-existing
      <code>wasp-and-1a-editable.svg</code>. A regression covers power
      exhaustion when generation is below baseline drain; collection cannot keep
      a depleted ship alive on a net loss.
    </p>
    <p>
      Full browser regression, backend/emulator checks and device performance
      were not run for this change. No publication or push is implied. The rate
      remains an alpha tuning choice.
    </p>
  </section>
</StudyLayout>
